// ch15 (finding D13): "A top-level `fn` annotates its parameters and
// return type in full" — yet `fn main with Console` has no return
// annotation anywhere in the book. Is the return annotation optional
// for ordinary functions too?
fn add(x: Int, y: Int) {
  x + y
}

fn main with Console {
  println("\{add(40, 2)}")
}
